NickelOS: explicit synchronization (linux-drm-syncobj-v1) for X11 clients
on NVIDIA, on by default (NICKEL_SOMMELIER_EXPLICIT_SYNC=0 turns it off).
Without it Xwayland on NVIDIA (no implicit sync) copies every frame an app
presents and waits for the GPU (glFinish) before presenting it; with it
Xwayland hands the app's buffers through with sync points. Exo has no
explicit sync, so sommelier keeps the promises, as compositors with
explicit sync do: a commit whose acquire point has not signaled is held,
its fence watched in the event loop, and goes to Exo once the rendering is
done. Nothing waits on a CPU meanwhile, and Exo never composites behind a
slow app (a GPU-side wait in Exo would hold the whole screen back). Any
other request for a surface with a held commit sends that commit on first.
A release point is signaled when Exo releases the buffer (after the GPU is
done with it). Apps without sync points are copied, not flipped (xwayland
r3). NICKEL_SOMMELIER_EXPLICIT_SYNC=test-nowait drops the synchronization,
for hw/x-sync-test.sh only.

